  "rationale": "The feasible Pareto front is well-established with 6 distinct designs covering the trade-off space effectively. The minimum area achieved is 6870 um^2 (iterative, data_width=15, n_iter=13), which is significantly below the HV reference of 40000 um^2. The accuracy constraint (max_abs_err <= 2^-10) is met by all front designs, with the best accuracy reaching 12.5 bits. Throughput constraints are comfortably satisfied (best 11.8 MSPS vs 1 MSPS requirement). The iterative family dominates the front, with unrolled_k showing higher area for comparable performance. Since this is the final round and the front covers the relevant region of the objective space (area 6870-9823 um^2, accuracy 10.2-12.5 bits) with clear trade-offs, stopping is appropriate. The selection rule (min area) would pick the 6870 um^2 design, which meets all constraints."
